    "narrative": "The cornerstone of our lineup today is **Lawrence Butler** (74.61), who earns the top slot against the vulnerable Dobnak. With a high-leverage matchup and favorable platoon dynamics boosting his base projection, he is a primary candidate for extra-base production. Similarly, **Jos\u00e9 Ram\u00edrez** (70.36) remains an anchor; despite a slight platoon drag, his elite talent profile and a favorable matchup against Roupp make him a locked-in must-start. **Jonathan Aranda** (67.95) and **Daulton Varsho** (65.74) also provide significant ceiling, as both benefit from advantageous matchups against Bieber and Rodriguez, respectively, with **Daulton Varsho**\u2019s outfield versatility remaining a key asset as we chase production across the board.\n\nThe most difficult decision was the final outfield slot, where **JJ Bleday** (53.26) and **Braden Montgomery** (52.92) were separated by less than half a point. Ultimately, we prioritized **JJ Bleday**\u2019s proven output, though his negative platoon variance against McGreevy was a concern. **Dylan Beavers** (55.70) remains in the lineup despite the daunting task of facing Gerrit Cole; his high park factor compensates for the SP skill deficit, providing enough floor to keep him active. Conversely, we are keeping a close eye on **Yainer Diaz** (54.88); his score is tempered by the uncertainty of the #9 hole in the lineup, yet his SP-skill advantage against Rodriguez makes him a defensible start given our internal depth. \n\nWe must remain vigilant regarding our \"Lineup Pending\" designations for **Yainer Diaz**, **Dylan Beavers**, and **Daulton Varsho**. Should official batting orders shift these players out of their anticipated slots, their daily efficiency scores will fluctuate; however, barring extreme drops, their matchups remain superior to our unavailable reserve options like **Bryce Harper** or the sidelined **Tyler Freeman**. While we lack the stolen base upside of players like **Justin Crawford** today, the current configuration maximizes our run-production potential against a slate of pitchers with high expected ERAs, particularly the favorable conditions facing **Lawrence Butler** and **Zack Gelof**.",
